Holistic review guidance:
- Review the assembled draft as a coherent candidate narrative, not as four
  unrelated keyword lists.
- Check direct, transferable, partial, and unsupported requirement matches.
- Check cross-section consistency of technologies, metrics, project names,
  dates, ownership, chronology, and candidate seniority.
- Inspect every evidence assignment, cross-entry source, impact inference basis,
  exact final claim, and final STAR sentence for plausibility and contradiction.
- Confirm exact work counts of 4/3/3 and exactly two bullets per project; every
  bullet must contain nonempty situation_task, action, result, text, provenance,
  and impact metadata.
- Check evidence density, semantic redundancy, generic language, causality,
  interview defensibility, readability, and ATS clarity.
- Check voice: structural variety within each role, verb strength against
  actual scope, concrete referents behind technical noun phrases, and whether
  every number on the page carries something to measure it against.
- Recommend a section replacement only when it is a complete, grounded,
  section-level improvement; never rewrite the resume monolithically.
